 # 8\. Phase 5 – READ ACL Planning

 The READ ACL is the primary security component of this project.

 ### Configuration

```
Type: Record
Operation: Read
Name: u_institution_details
Active: True
Advanced: True
Required Role: bb1
Data Condition: Branch is EEE
```

 The script will provide the administrator exception and additional role-based logic.

 ### Planned Decision Process

```
             User requests record
                     |
                     v
              Is user admin?
                /       \
              Yes        No
              |           |
            Allow      Has bb1?
                         /   \
                       Yes    No
                        |      |
                  Branch EEE   Deny
                    /    \
                  Yes     No
                   |       |
                 Allow    Deny
```

 ### Important Implementation Check

 The final implementation must ensure that the script itself does not accidentally bypass the Branch condition.

 For example, this logic:

```
if (gs.hasRole('bb1')) {
    return true;
}
```

 by itself means that every `bb1` user passes the script, regardless of Branch.

 Therefore, during implementation, the Branch condition must actually participate in the authorization decision if the requirement is **"EEE users can see only EEE records."**

 ### Deliverable

 A functioning READ ACL that enforces the intended record-level restriction.

